# Paperia SCSS

Use the modern Sass module system only:

- Always `@use` / `@forward`
- Never `@import`

## Structure

```
assets/scss/
├── abstracts/
│   ├── _variables.scss
│   ├── _colors.scss
│   ├── _mixins.scss
│   ├── _functions.scss
│   └── _breakpoints.scss
├── base/
│   ├── _reset.scss
│   ├── _typography.scss
│   └── _global.scss
├── layout/
│   ├── _header.scss
│   ├── _footer.scss
│   └── _grid.scss
├── components/
│   ├── _button.scss
│   ├── _card.scss
│   ├── _form.scss
│   ├── _hero.scss
│   └── _navigation.scss
├── pages/
│   ├── _home.scss
│   ├── _single.scss
│   └── _archive.scss
├── utilities/
│   ├── _helpers.scss
│   └── _spacing.scss
├── themes/
│   ├── _light.scss
│   └── _dark.scss
└── styles.scss
```

Every component lives in its own partial. Compile to `assets/css/styles.css` and enqueue that file.

## Light / dark theme

- Define semantic CSS custom properties (e.g. `--color-bg`, `--color-text`, `--color-accent`) in `_colors.scss`.
- Map light and dark values in `themes/_light.scss` and `themes/_dark.scss`.
- Apply via `[data-theme="light"]` / `[data-theme="dark"]` on `html` (or `body`). Prefer `color-scheme` alongside tokens.
- Respect `prefers-color-scheme` as the default when the user has no saved preference.
- Components consume tokens only — never hardcode light/dark hex values inside component partials.

```scss
// ❌ BAD
.card { background: #fff; color: #111; }

// ✅ GOOD
.card {
  background: var(--color-surface);
  color: var(--color-text);
}
```

## Variables

Colors, type scale, spacing, radii, and breakpoints live in abstracts. Do not scatter magic numbers in components.
